-- The field oracle rows (S8b, Q-S8b-7 (a)). Each row def compares one field op
-- of the domain file (feAdd, feSub, feMul, feInv on Fr and Fp) with the
-- value of the C oracle (test/cryptotool.c) and gives 1 when they are equal.
-- A row takes the inputs and then the expected value, each as 8 Words, least
-- significant first. The values are canonical: oMul puts the first input in
-- Montgomery form, so feMul gives the canonical product, and oInv takes the
-- inverse in Montgomery form. Each helper takes the modulus as a binder, and
-- each row def calls a helper at the head of its body: then the check does
-- not unroll feInv. This is a kit file outside the Wasm set: `langc --kit ir`
-- refuses frInv (EVAL_DEPTH). test/gate.sh evaluates each row with
-- `langc --kit eval`. oMulC compares the native feMulC (S8b2, Q-S8b-4 (a))
-- with the C oracle. It does not call feToMont, so the expected value is the
-- Montgomery product a b R^-1 mod m of the raw inputs, R = 2^256.
-- oPtGuest compares the native ptMulC (S8b2, Q-S8b2-1 (a)) with the guest
-- ptMul, and oPtMul compares ptMulC with g1_mul of the C oracle (Q-S8b2-8
-- (a)). The coordinates of a row are canonical: oPt puts them in Montgomery
-- form.
def oAdd : FeMod -> Fe -> Fe -> Fe -> Nat := fun (md : FeMod) (a : Fe) (b : Fe) (c : Fe) => either (fun (u : Unit) => 0) (fun (u : Unit) => 1) (feEq (feAdd md a b) c)
def oSub : FeMod -> Fe -> Fe -> Fe -> Nat := fun (md : FeMod) (a : Fe) (b : Fe) (c : Fe) => either (fun (u : Unit) => 0) (fun (u : Unit) => 1) (feEq (feSub md a b) c)
def oMul : FeMod -> Fe -> Fe -> Fe -> Nat := fun (md : FeMod) (a : Fe) (b : Fe) (c : Fe) => either (fun (u : Unit) => 0) (fun (u : Unit) => 1) (feEq (feMul md (feToMont md a) b) c)
def oInv : FeMod -> Fe -> Fe -> Nat := fun (md : FeMod) (a : Fe) (c : Fe) => either (fun (u : Unit) => 0) (fun (u : Unit) => 1) (feEq (feFromMont md (feInv md (feToMont md a))) c)
